\\\ P(X\\le 9) & =0.7734\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we transform to a standard normal random variable by $z$-scoring:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X\\le 9) & =0.7734 \\\\ P(Z\\le \\frac{9-0}{\\sigma }) & =0.7734 \\\\ Φ(\\frac{9}{\\sigma }) & =0.7734 \\\\ \\frac{9}{\\sigma } & ={Φ}^{-1}(0.7734)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAccording to the table, we have\n\n$$\nΦ(0.75)=0.7734\\,⇒\\,{Φ}^{-1}(0.7734)=0.75.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{9}{\\sigma } & =0.75 \\\\ \\sigma  & =\\frac{9}{0.75} \\\\ \\sigma  & =12.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sigma }^{2} & =(12)^{2}=144.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533433 17592186045585 true] [17592186120561 1068 #edb/ref 17592186119449 13194139533433 17592186045585 false] [17592186120561 1068 #edb/ref 17592186360408 13194139533433 17592186045585 true] [17592186120561 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533433 17592186045585 true] [17592186120561 1071 "Calculate\n$\\displaystyle \\int_{1}^{2}f(t)dt$\ngiven that\n$\\displaystyle \\int_{1}^{3}f(t)dt = ⟨ - 2, 3, 4⟩$\nand\n$\\displaystyle \\int_{2}^{3}f(t)dt = ⟨8,-6, 15⟩$." 13194139533433 17592186045585 false] [17592186120561 1071 "Calculate \n${\\int }_{1}^{2}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t$\ngiven that\n${\\int }_{1}^{3}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t=⟨-2,\\,3,\\,4⟩$\nand\n${\\int }_{2}^{3}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t=⟨8,\\,-6,\\,15⟩.$" 13194139533433 17592186045585 true] [17592186120561 1074 "Using the adjacent intervals rule, we have\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{1}^{3}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t={\\int }_{1}^{2}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t+{\\int }_{2}^{3}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nWe can rearrange the above as follows:\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{1}^{2}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t={\\int }_{1}^{3}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t-{\\int }_{2}^{3}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t\n$$\n\nFinally, using the given information, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{2}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t & ={\\int }_{1}^{3}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t-{\\int }_{2}^{3}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =⟨-2,\\,3,\\,4⟩-⟨8,\\,-6,\\,15⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-10,\\,9,\\,-11⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533433 17592186045585 tru