name{cosh}⁡x=\\frac{1}{2}({e}^{x}+{e}^{-x}).\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡4 & =\\frac{1}{2}({e}^{4}+{e}^{-4}).\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533433 17592186045585 true] [17592186360612 1068 #edb/ref 17592186360237 13194139533433 17592186045585 true] [17592186360612 1069 "q-95597" 13194139533433 17592186045585 true] [17592186360612 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533433 17592186045585 true] [17592186360612 1071 "Which of the following is equivalent to  $\\operatorname{tanh}⁡(-\\frac{1}{w})?$" 13194139533433 17592186045585 true] [17592186360612 1072 #uuid "c5805088-82e1-5cbe-a7b1-5d720f7c441d" 13194139533433 17592186045585 true] [17592186360612 1074 "The definition of $\\operatorname{tanh}⁡x$ is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{tanh}⁡x & =\\frac{{e}^{x}-{e}^{-x}}{{e}^{x}+{e}^{-x}} \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{2x}-1}{{e}^{2x}+1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1-{e}^{-2x}}{1+{e}^{-2x}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the third definition, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{tanh}⁡(-\\frac{1}{w}) & =\\frac{1-{e}^{-2(-1/w)}}{1+{e}^{-2(-1/w)}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1-{e}^{2/w}}{1+{e}^{2/w}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533433 17592186045585 true] [17592186360613 1068 #edb/ref 17592186360227 13194139533433 17592186045585 true] [17592186360613 1069 "q-95599" 13194139533433 17592186045585 true] [17592186360613 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533433 17592186045585 true] [17592186360613 1071 "Which of the following is equivalent to  $\\operatorname{tanh}⁡\\sqrt{u}?$" 13194139533433 17592186045585 true] [17592186360613 1072 #uuid "68943f94-9240-50e2-8b64-ff3ee0b816ca" 13194139533433 17592186045585 true] [17592186360613 1074 "The definition of $\\operatorname{tanh}⁡x$ is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{tanh}⁡x & =\\frac{{e}^{x}-{e}^{-x}}{{e}^{x}+{e}^{-x}} \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{2x}-1}{{e}^{2x}+1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1-{e}^{-2x}}{1+{e}^{-2x}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the second definition, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{tanh}⁡\\sqrt{u} & =\\f