lt, statements I and III are false, while statement II is true.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\"" 13194139533433 17592186045585 true] [17592186360724 1068 #edb/ref 17592186360154 13194139533433 17592186045585 true] [17592186360724 1069 "q-96829" 13194139533433 17592186045585 true] [17592186360724 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533433 17592186045585 true] [17592186360724 1071 "Given that $x,y\\in {C}^{3},$ compute the standard Hermitian inner product $⟨x,y⟩$ of the following two vectors.\n\n$$\nx=[\\begin{aligned}1-4\\text{i} \\\\ 1-6\\text{i} \\\\ \\text{i}\\end{aligned}],\\,y=[\\begin{aligned}\\text{i}+4 \\\\ \\text{i}+9 \\\\ -\\text{i}\\end{aligned}].\n$$" 13194139533433 17592186045585 true] [17592186360724 1072 #uuid "489acc36-31c7-57f2-a979-d95e2ad4a49e" 13194139533433 17592186045585 true] [17592186360724 1074 "Using the definition of the standard Hermitian inner product, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨x,y⟩ & ={x}_{1}\\overset{―}{{y}_{1}}+{x}_{2}\\overset{―}{{y}_{2}}+{x}_{3}\\overset{―}{{y}_{3}} \\\\  & =(1-4i)\\cdot (\\overset{―}{i+4})+(1-6i)\\cdot (\\overset{―}{i+9})+\\text{i}\\cdot (\\overset{―}{-\\text{i}}) \\\\  & =(1-4i)\\cdot (4-i)+(1-6i)\\cdot (9-i)+\\text{i}\\cdot \\text{i} \\\\  & =(-17i)+(3-55i)+(-1) \\\\  & =2-72i.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533433 17592186045585 true] [17592186360725 1068 #edb/ref 17592186360159 13194139533433 17592186045585 true] [17592186360725 1069 "q-96830" 13194139533433 17592186045585 true] [17592186360725 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533433 17592186045585 true] [17592186360725 1071 "![](images/74/740d578e554cd61bc733079c32c063d41ab4d9dcc775d36f7080ee8e5aa5a622.png)\n\nConsider the function $f:X\\to Y$ given by the mapping diagram shown above. Which of the following statements are true?\n\n- The domain of $f$ is ${5,10,15}$\n- The codomain of $f$ is ${5,10,12,13,14,15}$\n- The range of $f$ is ${12,13,14}$" 13194139533433 17592186045585 true] [17592186360725 1072 #uuid "9d79f788-f655-5287-8607-5b096289e0bd" 13194139533433 17592186045585 true] [17592186360725 1074 "The notation $f:X\\to Y$ means that the function $f$ maps the set $X$ to the set $Y.$ In this case,\n\n- the domain of $f$ is $X,$\n\n- the codomain of $f$ is $Y.$\n\nThe range of $f$ is the subset of the codomain that contains all values $y\\in Y$ that are mapped to by at least one element $x\\in X.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's inspect our diagram:\n\n- the domain of $f$ is $X={5,10,15},$\n\n- the codomain of $f$ is $Y={12,13,14},$\n\n- the range of $f$ is ${12,13},$ the subset of elements of $Y$ that have at least one incoming arrow.\n\nAs a result, statements II and III are false, while statement I is true.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer \"I only.\"" 13194139533433 17592186045585 true] [17592186360726 1068 #edb/ref 17592186360361 13194139533433 17592186045585 true] [17592186360726 1069 "q-96855" 13194139533433 17592186045585 true] [17592186360726 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533433 17592186045585 true] [17592186360726 1071 "Consider the linear transformation $T$ with matrix representation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}-4 & 2 \\\\ -8 & 4\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nA triangle $S$ has vertices at $(1,-1)$, $(1,0)$ and $(-2,1).$ Which of the following are coordinates of the vertices of ${S}^{′},$ the image of $S$ under the action of $T?$ \n\n- $(10,20)$\n- $(4,-8)$\n- $(-6,6)$" 13194139533433 17592186045585 true] [17592186360726 1072 #uuid "e1d4a0e7-8ceb-5003-89cd-d540839fd74d" 13194139533433 17592186045585 true] [17592186360726 1074 "To find the image of $S$ under the action of $T$, we first create a matrix $X$ containing all of the vertices of $S:$\n\n$$\nX=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & -2 \\\\ -1 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the image of $X$ under $T$ by calculating the matrix product $TX:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}TX & =[\\begin{aligned}-4 & 2 \\\\ -8 & 4\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & -2 \\\\ -1 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-6 & -4 & 10 \\\\ -12 & -8 & 20\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the respective vertices of ${S}^{′}$ are $(-6,-12)$, $(-4,-8)$ and $(10,20).$ \n\nSo, the correct answer is \"I  only.\"" 13194139533433 17592186045585 true] [17592186360727 1068 #edb/ref 17592186360216 13194139533433 17592186045585 true] [17592186360727 1069 "q-96856" 13194139533433 17592186045585 true] [17592186360727 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533433 17592186045585 true] [17592186360727 1071 "Consider the linear transformation $T$ with matrix representation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & -4\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nA triangle $S$ has vertices at $(0,-1),(1,1),$ and $(3,2).$ Which of the following are coordinates of the vertices of ${S}^{′},$ the image of $S$ under the action of $T?$\n\n- $(-1,4)$\n- $(-2,4)$\n- $(1,-3)$" 13194139533433 17592186045585 true] [17592186360727 1072 #uuid "0b46e610-7522-5441-8d91-b874b0e467ac" 13194139533433 17592186045585 true] [17592186360727 1074 "To find the image of $S$ under the action of $T$, we first create a matrix $X$ containing all of the vertices of $S:$\n\n$$\nX=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 & 3 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the image of $X$ under $T$ by calculating the matrix product $TX:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}TX & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & -4\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 & 3 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 4 & -2 & -2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the respective vertices of ${S}^{′}$ are  $(-2,4)$, and $(1,-2).$ \n\nSo, the correct answer is \" II only.\"" 13194139533433 17592186045585 true] [17592186360728 1068 #edb/ref 17592186360103 13194139533433 17592186045585 true] [17592186360728 1069 "q-96857" 13194139533433 17592186045585 true] [17592186360728 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533433 17592186045585 true] [17592186360728 1071 "Consider the linear transformation $T$ with matrix representation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 \\\\ 3 & 9\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nA triangle $S$ has vertices at $(0,-1),(-2,1),$ and $(3,0).$ Which of the following are coordinates of the vertices of ${S}^{′},$ the image of $S$ under the action of $T?$ \n\n- $(1,3)$\n- $(0,-3)$\n- $(2,3)$" 13194139533433 17592186045585 true] [17592186360728 1072 #uuid "ae6d946d-9a9f-5816-82c2-7048c4392f45" 13194139533433 17592186045585 true] [17592186360728 1074 "To find the image of $S$ under the action of $T$, we first create a matrix $X$ containing all of the vertices of $S:$\n\n$$\nX=[\\begin{aligned}0 & -2 & 3 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the image of $X$ under $T$ by calculating the matrix product $TX:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}TX & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 \\\\ 3 & 9\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 & -2 & 3 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 1 & 3 \\\\ -9 & 3 & 9\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the respective vertices of ${S}^{′}$ are $(-3,-9),$  $(1,3)$, and $(3,9).$ \n\nSo, the correct answer is \" I only.\"" 13194139533433 17592186045585 true] [17592186360729 1068 #edb/ref 17592186360349 13194139533433 17592186045585 true] [17592186360729 1069 "q-96863" 13194139533433 17592186045585 true] [17592186360729 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533433 17592186045585 true] [17592186360729 1071 "Approximate the value of $z$ such that $P(Z\\le z)=0.7900$ using interval bisection.\n\n| $z$ | $\\,0.00\\,$ | $\\,0.01\\,$ | $\\,0.02\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\,0.6\\,$ | $\\,0.7257\\,$ | $\\,0.7291\\,$ | $\\,0.7324\\,$ |\n| $\\,0.7\\,$ | $\\,0.7580\\,$ | $\\,0.7611\\,$ | $\\,0.7642\\,$ |\n| $\\,0.8\\,$ | $\\,0.7881\\,$ | $\\,0.7910\\,$ | $\\,0.7939\\,$ |" 13194139533433 17592186045585 true] [17592186360729 1072 #uuid "73caea9d-900f-5944-8b02-de7f34410a9e" 13194139533433 17592186045585 true] [17592186360729 1074 "First, we find the two numbers in the table that $0.7900$ lies between. These numbers are $0.7881$ and $0.7910.$ So, we have the following inequality:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}0.7881 & <0.7900<0.7910\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWriting the above inequality in terms of $Φ,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Φ(0.80) & <Φ(z)<Φ(0.81).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, using interval bisection, we can approximate $z$ as\n\n$$\nz≈\\frac{0.80+0.81}{2}=0.805.\n$$" 13194139533433 17592186045585 true] [17592186360730 1068 #edb/ref 17592186360132 13194139533433 17592186045585 true] [17592186360730 1069 "q-96935" 13194139533433 17592186045585 true] [17592186360730 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533433 17592186045585 true] [17592186360730 1071 "The table below gives the values of ${Φ}^{-1}(p)$ for different values of $p,$ where $p=Φ(z)$ is the cumulative distribution function for the standard normal distribution. Find the value of $z$ such that $P(Z\\le z)=0.80.$\n\n| $\\,p\\,$ | $0.65$ | $0.70$ | $0.75$ | $0.80$ | $0.85$ | $0.90$ | $0.95$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| ${Φ}^{-1}(p)$ | $\\,0.3853\\,$ | $\\,0.5244\\,$ | $\\,0.6745\\,$ | $\\,0.8416\\,$ | $\\,1.0364\\,$ | $\\,1.2816\\,$ | $\\,1.6449\\,$ |" 13194139533433 17592186045585 true] [17592186360730 1072 #uuid "19f27a3c-cd07-5bbe-b4b1-a15c2003039f" 13194139533433 17592186045585 true] [17592186360730 1074 "First, we express the given information in terms of $Φ:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(Z\\le z) & =0.80 \\\\ Φ(z) & =0.80\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we are looking for the value of $z$ such that\n\n$$\nz={Φ}^{-1}(0.80).\n$$\n\nWe look for the column in the table that corresponds to $p=0.80,$ and we find that\n\n$$\np=0.80\\,⇒\\,{Φ}^{-1}(p)=0.8416.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\nz={Φ}^{-1}(0.80)=0.8416.\n$$" 13194139533433 17592186045585 true] [17592186360731 1068 #edb/ref 17592186360288 13194139533433 17592186045585 true] [17592186360731 1069 "q-96936" 13194139533433 17592186045585 true] [17592186360731 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533433 17592186045585 true] [17592186360731 