e vertices of the triangle:\n\n$$\nX=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the image of $X$ under the action of $T$ by calculating the matrix product $TX:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}TX & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 & -2 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the image's vertices are $(-1,1)$, $(0,0),$ $(-2,2).$ Notice that all three points lie on the same line.\n\nSo, the image of our triangle under the action of $T$ is as follows:\n\n![](images/c2/c26cdc9a92481b7e2a7f9e128656d42c093b5fbb8d2ca4d02dc3bb262ce64341.png)" 13194139533433 17592186045585 true] [17592186360752 1068 #edb/ref 17592186360013 13194139533433 17592186045585 true] [17592186360752 1069 "q-97027" 13194139533433 17592186045585 true] [17592186360752 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533433 17592186045585 true] [17592186360752 1071 "Consider the matrix $T$ and the vector $v$ given below. If $T$ is the standard matrix of the linear transformation $T:{R}^{2}\\to {R}^{3},$ find $T(v).$\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}-4 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 1 \\\\ 3 & -5\\end{aligned}],\\,v=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]\n$$" 13194139533433 17592186045585 true] [17592186360752 1072 #uuid "92e50827-c106-565d-b3bc-40d269fedf11" 13194139533433 17592186045585 true] [17592186360752 1074 "Using the fact that $\\,T(v)=T\\cdot v,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(v) & =T\\cdot v \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-4 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 1 \\\\ 3 & -5\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 7 \\\\ -9\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533433 17592186045585 true] [17592186360753 1068 #edb/ref 17592186360402 13194139533433 17592186045585 true] [17592186360753 1069 "q-97061" 13194139533433 17592186045585 true] [17592186360753 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533433 17592186045585 true] [17592186